\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 received in both kinds simultaneously, in a manner approved by the\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 bishop.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 When the celebrant is assisted by a deacon or another priest, it is\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 customary for the celebrant to administer the consecrated Bread and the\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 assistant the Chalice. When several deacons or priests are present, some \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 may administer the Bread and others the Wine. In the absence of\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 sufficient deacons and priests, lay persons licensed by the bishop\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 according to the canon may administer the Chalice.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 If the consecrated Bread or Wine does not suffice for the number of\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 communicants, the celebrant is to return to the Holy Table, and\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 consecrate more of either or both, by saying\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs24 \f3 Hear us, O heavenly Father, and with thy (your) Word and\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 Holy Spirit bless and sanctify this bread (wine) that it, also,\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 may be the Sacrament of the precious Body (Blood) of thy\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 (your) Son Jesus Christ our Lord, who took bread (the cup)\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 and said, {\u8220\'93}This is my Body (Blood).{\u8221\'94}  }{\plain \fs24 \i\f3 Amen.}{\plain \fs22 \f3\fs22 \par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs22 \f3\fs22  }{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 or else the celebrant may consecrate more of both kinds, saying again the words of \softline
the Eucharistic Prayer, beginning with the words which follow \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 the Sanctus, and ending with the Invocation (in the case of Eucharistic \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 Prayer C, ending with the narrative of the Institution).\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 When the service of a priest cannot be obtained, the bishop may, at\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 discretion, authorize a deacon to distribute Holy Communion to the\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 congregation from the reserved Sacrament in the following manner:\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 1.  After the Liturgy of the Word (and the receiving of the people's\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 offering), the deacon reverently places the consecrated Sacrament on the\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 Altar, during which time a communion hymn may be sung.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 2.  The Lord's Prayer is then said, the deacon first saying, {\u8220\'93}Let us pray in \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 the words our Savior Christ hath (has) taught us.{\u8221\'94}\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 3.  And then, omitting the breaking of the Bread, the deacon proceeds\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 with what follows in the liturgy as far as the end of the postcommunion\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 prayer, and then dismisses the people.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 If any of the consecrated Bread or Wine remain, apart from any which\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 may be required for the Communion of the sick, or of others who for\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 \par
}\column 
\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 weighty cause could not be present at the celebration, or for the\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 administration of Communion by a deacon to a congregation when no priest is \softline
available, the celebrant or deacon, and other communicants,\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 reverently eat and drink it, either after the Communion of the people or\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 after the Dismissal.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 A hymn may be sung before or after the postcommunion prayer.\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \i\f3 Disciplinary Rubrics}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 \par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 If the priest knows that a person who is living a notoriously evil life\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 intends to come to Communion, the priest shall speak to that person\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 privately, and tell}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20  him}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  that }{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 he}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  may not come to the Holy Table until }{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 he}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 has given clear proof of repentance and amendment of life.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs22
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 The priest shall follow the same procedure with those who have done}{\plain \fs22 \f3\fs22 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 wrong to their neighbors and are a scandal to the other members of the\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 congregation, not allowing such persons to receive Communion until \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 they have made restitution for the wrong they have done, or have at least\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 promised to do so.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 When the priest sees that there is hatred between members of the\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 congregation, }{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 he}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  shall speak privately to each of them, telling them that \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 they may not receive Communion until they have forgiven each other. \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 And if the person or persons on one side truly forgive the others and \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 desire and promise to make up for their faults, but those on the other side\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 refuse to forgive, the priest shall allow those who are penitent to come to \softline
Communion, but not those who are stubborn.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 In all such cases, the priest is required to notify the bishop, within fourteen\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 days at the most, giving the reasons for refusing Communion.\par
}\pard \fs20
}